---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.4 · Slayer Backbone, Monkey Madness II & Theatre" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-4" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Slayer Backbone, Monkey Madness II &amp; Theatre</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Let required Slayer work supply combat XP, runes and cash before deciding how much standalone Magic training the account really needs.</p>
      </header>
      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Live cash/rune audit → Crafting 70 → Slayer 65 → Land of the Goblins → Slayer 69 → Grand Tree balloon + Monkey Madness II → Slayer 74 → A Night at the Theatre → allocate six combat rewards once → remaining Magic to 75."
        stats={["70 Crafting and 69 Slayer enter MM2", "74 Slayer is the later Blood Moon Rises gate", "75 Magic is the later DS2/DT2 gate; train its live remainder last"]}
        unlocks={["Royal seed pod, demonic gorillas and maniacal monkeys", "Land of the Goblins and A Night at the Theatre complete", "No fixed cash stack, black mask, Bowfa or rare crossbow required"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Slayer is scarce XP; Magic is flexible XP.</strong> Complete the mandatory Slayer intervals before allocating Duke's or the Theatre's selectable combat XP. A dust-devil task may train Magic while paying back part of its rune bill; another player's task sequence may not. Read the live account, not a projected Magic level.</div>
      <section><div class="section-label">Cash dependency · informational, not progress</div><h2>Audit what can actually pay for the next task.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Count now:</strong> liquid coins; immediately alchable items and nature runes; chaos, death, water, fire and air runes; any blood/soul runes; Prayer restores and food; Slayer points; banked glass, gems and battlestaff materials; and any already-owned black mask, Slayer helmet or rune crossbow. Keep an emergency quest/supply reserve. Do not convert the whole coin pile into thousands of Ancient casts. Withdraw or buy runes for a real task or modest batch, then check the resulting drops and balance.</div>
      <p><strong>Why the cash check matters:</strong> Chapter 2.1's 1,590 Earth battlestaves produced an estimated <strong>1,590 × 2,300 = 3,657,000 coins of gross staff/alch spread</strong> before rune/shop variation, not a guaranteed ending balance. Its first oak/teak plank stock alone cost roughly <strong>550,000–612,500 coins</strong> in conversion fees; the later actual-70 Construction stretch can need roughly <strong>500,000–750,000 more</strong> at 500 coins per additional teak plank. The route also names a 200,000-coin Iban upgrade, 130,000-coin Barrows gloves, 125,000-coin camphor hull, 25,000-coin Proselyte and house/quest purchases. <strong>Royal Trouble can draw up to 75,000 coins per day</strong>; a deposit is not an additional expense on top of its eventual draw. For a stress test, those named plank, gear and hull costs plus 2.1's roughly <strong>188,000 coins for the gold leaf and basic rooms</strong> total about <strong>1.72–2.03m</strong>. Add <strong>25 days × 75,000 = 1.875m</strong> of full kingdom draw and the illustrative outflow becomes <strong>3.59–3.91m</strong>—already near or above the entire staff spread <em>before</em> other quests, consumables or new income. Different plank stock, coffer days and Slayer/alch/Foundry income change the result. The guide therefore proves <strong>no fixed positive or negative Chapter 3 coin balance</strong>. Check the live coffer as well as the purse; if coins are tight, reduce or pause discretionary kingdom top-ups instead of spending the last quest/rune reserve. <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-1/`}>2.1 budget</a> · <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-3/`}>kingdom draw</a> · <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-6/`}>later planks</a>.</p>
      <p>For a small shortfall, alch <em>existing</em> useful drops with banked nature runes, do ordinary Slayer tasks, or turn banked/self-sourced metal into coins at Giants' Foundry; the account need not recreate a 35m cash stack. Preserve needed quest items rather than liquidating the bank indiscriminately. If a proposed rune batch exceeds spendable coins after the reserve, use a cheaper task/method and revisit after drops. <strong>Never count unalched loot as liquid coins.</strong></p>
      <ExpandableNote title="Why BRUHsailer's Chapter 3 cash number does not transfer" label="Source-route comparison">
        <p><a href="https://umkyzn.github.io/BRUHsailer/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current BRUHsailer</a> records roughly <strong>35.8m GP, 93 Magic and 59 Slayer</strong> around its Chapter 3 entry after a late Chapter 2 Hallowed Sepulchre/Fletchpalchre push toward 98 Agility. This guide deliberately skipped that long grind and its alching/cash return. BRUHsailer's later 100-combat, roughly 75-Slayer, 92-Ranged and CG goals explain its rune buying and Ranged-lamp choices, but cannot be imported into this account. We keep its useful macro insight—overlap required Slayer with combat training—without treating its 35m as ours.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section><div class="section-label">Close the MM2 gates</div><h2>Train only what the next quest consumes.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-crafting-70" number="1" title="Reach actual 70 Crafting for Monkey Madness II">
        <p>The Fremennik Exiles has already awarded its <strong>50,000 Crafting XP</strong>. At an exact actual-65 entry, <strong>449,428 + 50,000 = 499,428 XP</strong>; level 70 starts at <strong>737,627</strong>, leaving at most <strong>238,199 XP</strong> from that conservative floor. Read live XP and train only the remainder. Spend banked glass, gems, or remaining orb/staff materials first. Ordinary sand-and-soda-ash furnace glass is available; <strong>Superglass Make needs 77 Magic</strong>, which this route does not guarantee here. Do not buy a BRUHsailer-sized sand stock on credit.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="A cash-light alternative: Wyrmscraig Golem Crafting" label="Method choice, not another requirement">
          <p>After Fallen From Grace, sail or use its unlocked Wyrmscraig travel to <strong>Auchrie on Wyrmscraig</strong> and go to the nearby sunstone mine/golem plinths. Bring a pickaxe, hammer and chisel. Mine <strong>five sunstones per golem</strong>: four start the base at an empty plinth, while the fifth is chiselled into its core. Shape the four sides, then insert the core and one suitable Hunter fur; the finished golem yields Crafting XP and an uncut gem. Wyrmscraig goat fur can be hunted on the island, so rare furs or cash purchases are not prerequisites. The quieter loop uses the sunstone monolith and normal shaping clicks; moving between individual rocks for momentum and clicking to speed shaping is the active alternative. A goat-fur golem gives about <strong>2,440 Crafting XP</strong>, so an exact-floor 238,199-XP gap is on the order of <strong>98 golems</strong> before gems/other Crafting XP—not a fixed quota. It trades gathering time for minimal GP expense. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Golem_crafting" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current activity and material guide</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Use whichever material bank and pace suit you. <strong>Stop at actual, unboosted 70 Crafting.</strong></p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-slayer-65" number="2" title="Train live Slayer to actual 65; unlock dust devils">
        <p>At the conservative post-Exiles floor, Slayer is <strong>323,742 XP</strong>; actual 65 begins at <strong>449,428 XP</strong>, a maximum <strong>125,686-XP</strong> bridge before incidental task XP. Take normal assignments from a sensible master for your <em>actual</em> combat level; do not train combat simply to unlock a different master. Dragon scimitar/defender, Fire Cape, Piety, Barrows gloves and defensive/prayer gear already support ordinary melee tasks; the Arkan blade is situational. Bank alchables, runes, herbs and useful supplies. An already-owned black mask or Slayer helmet is welcome, but Cave Horror farming is an optional resumable detour, not a gate. Stop at actual 65.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="When should I mage a Slayer task?" label="Optional method decision">
          <p><strong>Dust devils unlock at 65 Slayer.</strong> On a naturally assigned task, the multicombat <strong>Catacombs of Kourend</strong> are the non-Wilderness default: buy/wear a <strong>facemask from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> unless an already-owned Slayer helmet protects you, gather/stack the devils, keep Prayer and health under control, and burst the stack. At route Magic 67+, <strong>Smoke Burst</strong> is available (<strong>4 chaos, 2 death, 2 air, 2 fire</strong> per cast); at actual 70 Magic, <strong>Ice Burst</strong> is the stronger ordinary choice (<strong>4 chaos, 2 death, 4 water</strong> per cast). Shadow Burst and Blood Burst cost more for this routine, while Blood's healing can be situational. A first <strong>200-cast batch</strong> is at most 800 chaos and 400 death runes, plus the matching elemental runes; count banked stock before buying. Alch/keep the drops; dust-devil loot often offsets much of the supply bill, but task and drop RNG make net profit unguaranteed. Melee ordinary single-target tasks; burst other naturally assigned, stackable multi-target tasks when practical. Do not spend a large Slayer-point balance forcing dust devils, Wilderness-burst by default, or burn Ancient runes on a task where their area damage gains little. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dust_devil" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Dust-devil protection/locations</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Slayer_task/Dust_devils" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Task methods</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-land-goblins" number="3" title="Quest break: complete Land of the Goblins">
        <p>Talk to <strong>Grubfoot at the Dorgesh-Kaan mine entrance</strong>, then escort him to Zanik/Oldak in the city. The Another Slice of H.A.M./Fishing Contest quest chain and the actual Agility, Fishing, Thieving and Herblore gates are already covered. Bank-check a safe light source, <strong>toadflax potion (unf), goblin mail (several pieces), yellow/blue/orange/purple dyes</strong>, an empty vial and pestle for black-mushroom dye, fishing rod, raw slimy eel and a few coins. Goblin mail and the black mushroom can be obtained during the quest. Bring a fairy-ring staff, Dorgesh-Kaan spheres/teleports, and ordinary combat gear/food for the temple encounters; bank between the Dorgesh-Kaan, Goblin Village and Goblin Cave/temple phases rather than carrying every disguise at once. Clear inventory/equipment when the goblin transformation requires it; do not bring a following pet into the temple. Claim <strong>8,000 XP each in Agility, Fishing, Thieving and Herblore</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Land_of_the_Goblins" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest items and phases</a>.</p>
        <p>This is a current Quest Cape quest and a breather from Slayer. <strong>Hopespear's Will is a separate, optional miniquest</strong>, not a required continuation here.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-slayer-69" number="4" title="Continue Slayer from actual 65 to actual 69 before MM2">
        <p>Actual 65 starts at <strong>449,428 XP</strong> and 69 at <strong>668,051 XP</strong>: a <strong>218,623-XP</strong> exact-floor interval. Use normal tasks and keep the cash/rune ledger current. Burst suitable naturally occurring assignments—Smoke Burst before Magic 70, Ice Burst afterward—while melee remains sensible for single targets. Do not force Magic onto every task or force a dust-devil assignment. <strong>Stop at actual 69 Slayer</strong>; MM2's fixed 80,000 Slayer XP should land before any more Slayer grinding.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Grandmaster quest · phased preparation</div><h2>Unlock the balloon destination, then finish Monkey Madness II.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-mm2" number="5" title="Verify the Grand Tree balloon route and complete Monkey Madness II">
        <p><strong>Balloon preflight:</strong> Enlightened Journey alone is not enough: the <strong>Gnome Stronghold/Grand Tree destination must actually be unlocked</strong> before MM2 begins. At the Entrana balloon, bank all weapons and armour, bring <strong>three magic logs</strong>, and unlock the route with actual <strong>60 Firemaking</strong> (already cleared). Chapter 1 targeted 16 magic logs: 12 for Desert Treasure I, one for Mourning's End I and these three. Check the destination and bank first; if it is already unlocked, do nothing. If logs are short, use any existing Wintertodt/Hunter reward logs first. For a reproducible shortfall at the guaranteed actual-70 Woodcutting floor, take a <strong>brown-spice spicy stew</strong> to a magic tree and repeat until its visible <strong>+5 Woodcutting</strong> boost lets you cut only the missing logs; the boost roll and individual log timing vary, but this avoids imposing an entire 70→75 Woodcutting grind. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Balloon_transport_system" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Balloon unlocks</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Spicy_stew" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Brown-spice boost</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Hard gate:</strong> actual <strong>69 Slayer, 70 Crafting, 60 Hunter, 55 Agility, 55 Thieving and 60 Firemaking</strong>, plus Enlightened Journey <em>and its Gnome route</em>, The Eyes of Glouphrie, RFD Freeing King Awowogei/Monkey Madness I, Troll Stronghold and Watchtower. The previous chapters cover the quest chain and other levels. Start with <strong>King Narnode in the Grand Tree</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_II/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current phase/item guide</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stage the story items:</strong> first a <strong>lemon, grapes, pestle and mortar, translation book</strong> (reclaim from Narnode if lost), and ordinary logs for Entrana; leave weapons/armour in the bank for that visit. On Ape Atoll, take the <strong>M'speak amulet, ninja monkey greegree, monkey talisman and light source</strong>, plus anti-poison, food and a one-click exit. The dangerous Kruk dungeon has an Agility route with failures into aggressive monkeys, or a tanking route needing a <strong>pickaxe and slash weapon</strong>. Unlock its return shortcut, then bank/regear for Kruk; take his paw to Zooknock for a Kruk greegree. Later phases revisit Kob at Troll Stronghold and Keef at Gu'Tanoth (bring the phase's small coin cost), then use the quest's satchels in the airship/laboratory. Follow the linked map for individual obstacles; do not carry every phase's inventory at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Combat floor:</strong> melee with dragon scimitar (Arkan only where suitable), dragon defender, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and normal defensive gear. Range with the Chapter 3.3 <strong>adamant crossbow or an already-owned RCB</strong>, remaining plain/enchanted bolts, Ava's accumulator and banked d'hide. Bring food, Prayer restores, poison cures, energy/stamina if available and a teleport. For <strong>Kruk</strong>, Protect from Missiles against his hard ranged hit and range/kite or carefully flinch from the wall; maintain a safe health margin because his melee still hurts. <strong>Kob/Keef</strong> hit hard even through prayer: use the matching protection, move, eat and regear between them. In the lab, clear the required <strong>tortured gorillas</strong>, then the <strong>two mandatory demonic gorillas</strong> by watching their protection prayers and attack styles, switching between the guaranteed melee/ranged kit. These two are quest fights, not permission to farm a zenyte.</p>
        <p><strong>Glough's three rooms:</strong> use the door/hallway to range his melee-only first phase. Lure the second phase back toward the first room's wall for the documented ranged safespot. <strong>Restock before entering the third phase</strong>; it can hit extremely hard and pull you into melee distance. With the guaranteed crossbow, keep high HP, Protect from Magic at range (Melee when forced adjacent), fire a controlled shot, then move back toward the previous chamber; repeat rather than tanking repeated pulls. A slower hit-and-retreat flinch can be learned from the linked strategy if supplies are low. A 10-square long-range weapon is an <em>optional</em> advanced safespot, not the baseline. Leaving or dying during Glough resets his phases; instanced unprotected items go to a grave outside, and items dropped on the floor are lost. Do not treat quest death as a safe minigame death. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Glough phases, death and rewards</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim the <strong>fixed 80,000 Slayer, 60,000 Agility, 50,000 Thieving and 50,000 Hunter XP</strong>, plus the reusable <strong>Royal seed pod</strong> and new gorilla/maniacal-monkey access. At the exact 69-Slayer floor, <strong>668,051 + 80,000 = 748,051 XP</strong>, already past level 70's <strong>737,627 XP</strong>. Record live Slayer XP. <strong>Leave Duke's two selectable 50,000-combat-XP rewards unclaimed</strong> until after the next Slayer block and Theatre. Duke's choices are Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic—<strong>not Slayer</strong>. No black mask, whip, zenyte, Bowfa, crystal armour, blowpipe or RCB drop is part of this outcome.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i34-slayer-74" number="6" title="Use post-MM2 Slayer to reach actual 74, then re-audit cash and runes">
        <p><strong>The Blood Moon Rises later consumes actual 74 Slayer</strong>. Claiming MM2 first makes the conservative remainder <strong>1,096,278 − 748,051 = 348,227 Slayer XP</strong>; read live XP and train only that gap. Continue ordinary tasks, burst suitable multicombat assignments and melee ordinary targets. This long interval can supply Magic XP, alchables, coins, runes, herbs and combat levels. No fixed dust-devil task count, black mask, 100-combat detour or level-75 Slayer target is imposed. <strong>Stop at actual 74.</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Second informational audit:</strong> now record live Magic XP, liquid coins, alchables, chaos/death/elemental/blood/soul runes, Prayer restores and food. Compare to the opening snapshot before planning the final Magic method. A lucky burst-task sequence and an all-melee sequence are both valid accounts; neither inherits BRUHsailer's cash or Magic level.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest break · learn the Theatre</div><h2>Complete the current story, then Entry Mode.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-night-theatre" number="7" title="Complete A Night at the Theatre after Slayer 74">
        <p><strong>This is more than a raid queue.</strong> With A Taste of Hope already complete, talk to the <strong>Mysterious Stranger at Ver Sinhaza</strong>; use Drakan's medallion and bank between investigations. Bring the retained <strong>Ivandis or blisterwood flail, saw, ghostspeak amulet and an axe</strong>. Investigate Ranis Drakan's grave, kill the required vyrewatch, inspect the spider-egg cave without attempting to kill its high-Slayer araxytes, carry antipoison for venom and leave the cave safely. Then visit <strong>Filliman at the Nature Grotto</strong> (fairy ring BIP), cross the swamp to the quest Hespori and fight it with food, antipoison and your ordinary combat kit. A druid pouch protects food from ghasts. Chop the defeated plant for bark and return to the Stranger; only then is the Theatre handoff ready. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Night_at_the_Theatre" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current reworked quest</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Entry Mode</strong> at Ver Sinhaza is substantially gentler than normal Theatre and allows unlimited room retries; it is a learning run, not a unique-item farm. Take three attack styles: scimitar/defender/Fire Cape and a <strong>poisoned dragon dagger</strong> or other poison weapon, the adamant crossbow or banked RCB/Ava/d'hide, and an affordable Magic spell/runes. If no poisoned dagger is banked, buy a plain dragon dagger from <strong>Jukat's shop in Zanaris</strong> (Lost City is complete) and apply <strong>weapon poison</strong>; actual 70 Herblore can make the basic poison from a kwuarm potion (unf) and dragon scale dust if none is banked. Bring real food, Prayer restores, poison cure and <strong>insulated boots for solo Verzik</strong>. Entry supply chests offer bandages after Bloat and Sotetseg; these heal and restore/boost resources, and failures give further supplies. Take what each room needs rather than treating a failed attempt as a reason to buy raid gear. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Theatre_of_Blood/Entry_Mode" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Entry equipment, supplies and room mechanics</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Six-room primer:</strong> at <strong>Maiden</strong>, Protect from Magic and move off blood pools. At <strong>Bloat</strong>, use pillars/line of sight, move with him and attack only during safe downtime. At <strong>Nylocas</strong>, match grey/melee, green/Ranged and blue/Magic, protect the pillars, and do not keep attacking a spider with the wrong style. At <strong>Sotetseg</strong>, react to prayer-colored attacks and follow the revealed maze path. At <strong>Xarpus</strong>, move off poison, manage the poison phase, then avoid attacking when he turns to stare. At <strong>Verzik</strong>, use the provided <strong>Dawnbringer</strong> for phase one, move between pillar cover and attack windows, then manage bombs/electric ball (solo insulated boots), kill the <strong>purple healing Nylocas with poison</strong>, and adapt prayers/movement as phases change. Use the linked exact-room guide for patterns; this is a first-pass plan, not a 63-wave-style script.</p>
        <p><strong>Death rules:</strong> Entry Mode's 2023 changes removed its 100,000-coin reclaim fee and allow unlimited retries, but deaths are <strong>dangerous for Hardcore Ironman and Hardcore Group Ironman status</strong>. Ordinary accounts may retry, but should still reclaim items promptly before another unsafe death. Do not call it a universally safe activity. After finishing the Entry run, return to the Stranger and complete the quest. Its four <strong>20,000-combat-XP lamps</strong> are held for Step 8. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Item_Retrieval_Service" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Entry reclaim fee</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Theatre_of_Blood" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hardcore death rule</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Allocate once · then close Magic</div><h2>Spend only the reward XP the live account needs.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i34-magic-75" number="8" title="Resolve the six combat rewards, then reach actual 75 Magic">
        <p><strong>Only now read live Magic XP, coins and runes.</strong> Duke holds <strong>2 × 50,000</strong> selectable combat XP; A Night offers <strong>4 × 20,000</strong> lamps, for <strong>180,000 total</strong> across six distinct claims. Eligible skills are Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged and Magic; <strong>Slayer is not a choice</strong>. If Magic is already 75+, default all six rewards to <strong>Strength</strong> (or Attack/another eligible combat skill if your account has a clearer need). If Magic is short, calculate the gap and consider how much cash/rune training it would displace: use 20k lamps first for a small gap, and one or both 50k Duke rewards on Magic only if the remaining gap and cash bank justify them. Put unused rewards into Strength by default. Mark all six rewards claimed <em>once</em>; do not allocate the same lamp in two projected skill budgets. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Monkey_Madness_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Duke reward</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Night_at_the_Theatre" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Theatre lamps</a>.</p>
        <p>After chosen rewards, <strong>remaining Magic XP = max(0, 1,210,421 − live Magic XP)</strong>. This is the actual-75 threshold for later Dragon Slayer II / Desert Treasure II, not a precomputed 482k bill. Train only this remainder. Three cash-aware lanes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Existing alchables:</strong> High Alch useful banked/Slayer drops with banked nature runes on the standard spellbook. This converts existing stock to liquid coins and Magic XP; do not manufacture an arbitrary mountain of alchables.</li>
          <li><strong>Cheap and quieter:</strong> Fire Bolt with the Family Crest <strong>chaos gauntlets</strong> on a suitable low-risk crab or Slayer target. Each cast uses <strong>one chaos, four fire and three air runes</strong>; a fire staff removes the fire-rune input. Gauntlets raise the base max hit from 12 to 15. Expect roughly <strong>35k–50k Magic XP/hour</strong> on a low-defence target with ordinary autocasting, varying with hit rate and interruptions. It is slower than bursting but costs far less per cast and can be done in modest batches. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fire_Bolt" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Spell and runes</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Fast, cash-sensitive:</strong> after MM2, maniacal monkeys in <strong>Kruk's Dungeon</strong> stack densely and drop one-dose Prayer potions. Protect from Melee, gather a stack and Ice Burst at actual 70+ Magic. Around <strong>1,000 casts/hour</strong> consumes about <strong>4,000 chaos, 2,000 death and 4,000 water runes/hour</strong>; at a rough 800–1,000 GP-equivalent per cast that is <strong>~0.8–1.0m rune value/hour</strong> before shop-price variation, while good stacks can yield roughly <strong>200k–300k Magic XP/hour</strong>. These are planning rates, not an invoice: test a small batch against live supply and stop when the XP target is met. Do not assume Barrage. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Maniacal_monkey/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Monkey method</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ice_Burst" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Spell runes</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Stop at actual 75 Magic.</strong> The goal is the quest gate, not a purchased 93-Magic analogue of BRUHsailer.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.4 complete · guaranteed route exit</div>
        <h3>The scarce Slayer work is done before the final Magic purchase decision.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Skills:</strong> actual 70+ Crafting, 74+ Slayer and 75+ Magic; no 75-Slayer or 77-Magic promise.</li>
          <li><strong>Quests/unlocks:</strong> Land of the Goblins, Grand Tree balloon destination, Monkey Madness II and A Night at the Theatre complete; Royal seed pod and gorilla/maniacal-monkey access obtained; fixed MM2 80k Slayer XP claimed.</li>
          <li><strong>Rewards:</strong> Duke's two 50k and Theatre's four 20k combat rewards resolved exactly once after the live Magic audit.</li>
          <li><strong>Carry forward:</strong> Fire Cape, deterministic ranged kit, remaining bolts, and a <em>re-audited</em> cash/rune bank—not a fictional fixed balance. Black mask/Slayer helmet, whip, zenytes, gorilla uniques, RCB RNG, Bowfa/crystal, blowpipe, Rigour and Ava's assembler remain optional.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <div class="subchapter-pager"><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-3/`}>← 3.3</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}intermediate/`}>Back to Intermediate overview</a></div>
    </article>
